Fix: use RenderDoc only when it is already in the process (not whenever it is installed)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0016-renderdoc-only-when-attached.patch
Status:     upstream bug (report to rexglue-sdk)

WHAT BROKE
  With RenderDoc installed (1.45), the game window never appeared on a
  Wayland desktop. The game ran normally
  behind it (logs: quick load, ~118 fps) and both the launcher and
  tools/play.sh were affected. Every log from then on said "RenderDoc API
  initialized", and the Vulkan instance had lost VK_KHR_wayland_surface
  (only VK_KHR_xcb_surface left).

WHY
  RenderDocAPI::CreateIfConnected() (src/ui/renderdoc_api.cpp) is meant to
  pick up RenderDoc only when it is attached. Its comment says "if not attached,
  the load will fail", but the code did a plain dlopen("librenderdoc.so"). With
  RenderDoc installed that load succeeds, which puts RenderDoc into every run.
  RenderDoc does not support Wayland and hides the Wayland surface extension,
  so the SDL Wayland window never gets a buffer and the compositor never maps it.
  Upstream Xenia checks with GetModuleHandle / RTLD_NOLOAD instead.

FIX
  First ask whether the library is ALREADY loaded (RTLD_NOW | RTLD_NOLOAD on
  POSIX, GetModuleHandleA on Windows); return nullptr if not. Only then Load()
  it (which just adds a reference). Starting the game from RenderDoc still
  works as before.

HOW FOUND
  The session logs were compared before and after the RenderDoc install
  (pacman.log): the first session after it had the "RenderDoc API initialized"
  line and no wayland_surface. That line was traced to the SDK.
  Test: with RenderDoc still installed, a launch logs no RenderDoc line, the
  Wayland surface is back, and the window is mapped (hyprctl clients).

diff --git a/src/ui/renderdoc_api.cpp b/src/ui/renderdoc_api.cpp
index e1a5287..9b140a3 100644
--- a/src/ui/renderdoc_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/renderdoc_api.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,18 @@
 #include <rex/logging.h>
 #include <rex/ui/renderdoc_api.h>
 
+#if REX_PLATFORM_WIN32
+#ifndef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#endif
+#ifndef NOMINMAX
+#define NOMINMAX
+#endif
+#include <windows.h>
+#elif !REX_PLATFORM_MAC
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#endif
+
 namespace rex {
 namespace ui {
 
@@ -25,9 +37,24 @@ std::unique_ptr<RenderDocAPI> RenderDocAPI::CreateIfConnected() {
 
   pRENDERDOC_GetAPI get_api = nullptr;
 
-  // Try to load the RenderDoc library. If RenderDoc is attached, the library
-  // should already be loaded into the process and this will increment the
-  // reference count. If not attached, the load will fail and we return nullptr.
+  // Only use RenderDoc when it is ALREADY in the process (the game was started
+  // from RenderDoc, or its Vulkan layer was enabled). A plain load would pull
+  // librenderdoc in on every machine that merely has RenderDoc installed, and
+  // RenderDoc then hides the Wayland surface extension: the window never gets a
+  // picture and the compositor never shows it. So ask "is it loaded?" first
+  // (RTLD_NOLOAD / GetModuleHandle, like upstream Xenia); the Load() below then
+  // only adds a reference to the copy that is already there.
+#if REX_PLATFORM_WIN32
+  if (!GetModuleHandleA(platform::lib_names::kRenderDoc)) {
+    return nullptr;
+  }
+#else
+  void* already_loaded = dlopen(platform::lib_names::kRenderDoc, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_NOLOAD);
+  if (!already_loaded) {
+    return nullptr;
+  }
+  dlclose(already_loaded);  // drop the probe's reference; Load() takes its own
+#endif
   if (!renderdoc_api->library_.Load(platform::lib_names::kRenderDoc)) {
     return nullptr;
   }
